<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco cuts Gulf A-960 bunkers by $7/tonne.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts Gulf A-960 bunkers by $7/tonne.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has cut A-960 bunker fuel oil from Ras Tanura and Damman by $7 a tonne to $119 a tonne ($18.27 a barrel) with effect September 12, Aramco said.</p>
<p>A-960 prices from Jeddah and Yanbu are left unchanged at $120 a tonne ($18.42 a barrel).</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from all four ports is $1 lower at $204 a tonne.</p>
</text>
